    {
      "slot": 13,
      "native": {
        "slot": 13,
        "native_line": 842,
        "native_literal": "\\triv",
        "raw_line_sha256": "27e8dff7044f59c06fc48df4e774d095fbcf6b54c6c18f6b83cdb7b1448a8298",
        "context": "  By Schur's lemma, $\\rho$ defines a character of the center $$\\lambda:Z(G) \\to \\C^{\\times}, \\;\\, z\\mapsto \\lambda(z),$$ where $\\rho(z) = \\lambda(z)\\id$. Since $\\rho^* \\cong \\rho$, we have: $\\triv \\subset \\rho \\otimes \\rho^* \\cong \\rho^{\\otimes 2}$ and on this space $z \\in Z(G)$ acts by $\\lambda^2(z)\\id$. So $\\lambda(z)^2 = 1$ and thus $\\lambda(z)=\\pm 1$. Now, since $\\rho$ is faithful, the map $\\lambda: Z(G) \\to \\C$ is injective, hence $Z(G) \\subset C_2 $."
      },
      "source": {
